<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50377" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴλιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑλ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ἡ</span>,
			<u>Ilios</u> or <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Ilium, the city of Ilus, Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.210
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				8.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				103
			</span></i> (eleg.): <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴλιον</span></b> ,
				τό, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.71
			</span></i>, but always in Trag. (exc. E.l.c.):—hence 
				Ep.
			 genitives, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλιόθεν</span></b> , <i>from Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.251
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.39
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλιόθι</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρό</span>
			<i>before Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.581
			</span></i>, etc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰλιόφι</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλυτὰ τείχεα</span> the walls <i>of
			Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.295
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
			Adj., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴλιος</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
				<i>Ilian, Trojan</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθάνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					1008
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span> is f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1164
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
